SUMMARY:Swimming Home — Documentary World Premiere + Q&A
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T190000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:dothebay-17900448@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:A feature documentary about one man's solo swim across the Eng
 lish Channel — and the promise to his mother that drove it.\n\n100% of t
 icket sales go to cancer research at Gustave Roussy\, Europe's leading can
 cer research and treatment centre\, in France.\n\nSwimming Home is a featu
 re documentary about one man's attempt to swim the English Channel — sol
 o\, without a wetsuit\, across 21 miles of cold\, unpredictable water know
 n as the "Everest of swims."\n\nThe film follows Erwan Le Roy\, a French-b
 orn San Franciscan with no endurance-swimming background\, over the year h
 e spends transforming himself\, body and mind\, for a crossing most people
  would never attempt. What starts as a promise to his mother after her can
 cer diagnosis becomes a true story about grief\, hope\, and what it takes 
 to keep going when every reason to quit is right there in the water.\n\nWo
 rld Premiere\, followed by a live Q&A with Erwan Le Roy\, the swimmer at t
 he center of the film.\nDocumentary · 74 minutes. Doors 5:00pm — screen
 ing begins promptly at 5:30pm — Q&A to follow. Event ends 7:30pm.\n\n$23
 .18\n\nTickets: https://consumer.pxf.io/APvP5J?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.eventbr
 ite.com%2Fe%2Fswimming-home-documentary-world-premiere-qa-with-erwan-le-ro
 y-tickets-1999712369528\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/13/s
 wimming-home-documentary-world-premiere-q-a-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay\n\nA
 lso listed on:\n- https://sf.funcheap.com/swimming-home-documentary-world-
 premiere-qa/
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34697572/f5ff27a1-12c9-4634-ad19-accab3c0a722.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:Marina Theater\, 2149 Chestnut St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94123
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/13/swimming-home-documentary-world
 -premiere-q-a-tickets
