BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Halloween (1978)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261031T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261031T180000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17830869@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:In 1978\, legendary New Yorker film critic Pauline Kael review
 ed John Carpenter's HALLOWEEN. She didn’t like it.\n\n"HALLOWEEN has a p
 itiful\, amateurish script (by Carpenter and his producer\, Debra Hill). A
 n escaped lunatic wielding a kitchen knife stalks people in a small Midwes
 tern town (Haddonfield\, Illinois)\, and that's about it. Maybe when a hor
 ror film is stripped of everything but dumb scariness – when it isn't as
 hamed to revive the stalest device of the genre (the escaped lunatic) – 
 it satisfies part of the audience in a more basic\, childish way than soph
 isticated horror pictures do."\n\nEternal respect to Ms. Kael\, but what s
 he disdained more than 40 years ago are the very elements that have made t
 his film endure for over four decades.\n\nHALLOWEEN might not have resembl
 ed the “sophisticated” horror films of the 1970s\, but the simplicity 
 of the film’s story and production values allowed Carpenter to focus on 
 staying one step ahead of the audience. From Dean Cundey's flowing\, blue-
 hued photography to Carpenter's minimalist score to the blank\, ominous ma
 sk of Michael Myers\, nothing in this moody\, terrifying film is misplaced
 .\n\nJust as BLAZING SADDLES\, DIE HARD\, and THE MATRIX reinvigorated the
 ir genres by satisfying in “basic\, childish ways\,” Carpenter created
  a pitch-perfect prototype in HALLOWEEN that changed an entire genre forev
 er.\n\nTickets: https://drafthouse.com/sf/show/halloween-1978?cinemaId=080
 2&sessionId=21355\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/31/hallowe
 en-1978-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7562198;-122.419185
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34368059/a85735fd-914d-48c0-a4b5-d13b20b5d2ba.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003107Z
LOCATION:Alamo Drafthouse Cinema\, 2550 Mission St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 
 94110
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/31/halloween-1978-tickets
END:VEVENT
